Implement SCR-002-plans. Do not do any simulation or calculation backend yet, just use sensible placeholder values. Do default tab only.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The Plans toolbar button opens the Plan Browser as a bottom sheet.
- [x] The Default tab contains all nine fixed plans from SCR-002.
- [x] Each row shows summary statistics and turn 1–10 probability columns.
- [x] Placeholder statistics are visibly red.
- [x] Custom plans, graph navigation, and simulation remain out of scope.
- [x] `REQ-008-scroll` implemented.
- [ ] Relevant automated checks pass.
- [x] Placeholder statistics should be realistic. i.e. p(5) >= p(4).

## Implementation notes

- `PlanBrowserView` is presented from the existing Plans toolbar button with a large sheet detent and drag indicator.
- `DefaultPlan.placeholders` contains the fixed design order and deterministic placeholder statistics.
- The table is split into a fixed corner, horizontally synchronized headers, a vertically synchronized plan column, and a two-axis scrolling values viewport.
- The values viewport is the single source of scroll offsets; separate clipped header and plan panes follow only their relevant axis.
- Opaque fixed panes and explicit group dividers prevent values from appearing behind the plan column and clearly separate summary statistics from probabilities.
- Fixed and scrolling panes share explicit 44-point rows and 1-point separators; normalized scroll insets keep their vertical offsets aligned.
- The values pane uses a top-leading default anchor and top-aligned minimum viewport height, preventing short result sets from being vertically centered away from their plan rows.
- The plan and summary columns are compact enough to show Mean, Median, 25th, and 75th simultaneously at common iPhone widths.
- Table separators use a slightly stronger secondary tint for clearer grouping.
- Super-column headers group turn summaries and cumulative completion probabilities.
- Placeholder probabilities use a monotonic cumulative distribution so each later-turn probability is at least the preceding value.
- Custom and graph controls are visible but unavailable until their separate screens are specified and implemented.

## Evidence

- Added unit coverage for the fixed plan order and ten probability values per row.
- Added unit coverage requiring cumulative probabilities to be bounded and nondecreasing.
- Added UI coverage for opening, inspecting, scrolling, and closing the Plan Browser, including assertions for the structurally separate fixed column and headers.
- Added UI coverage comparing the first plan and result row midpoints within a 1.5-point tolerance.
